## 6. Reader Standard — met

No oaths; the one swearing is "a perfectly clean word" through a wall (ch2:235). Violence costs and is felt without gore: the lever in the shoulder "a hot tearing pull… as if a thick cord had been drawn too tight", the forearm "purple by morning", Karis's palms "as though she had leaned them on a stove", the left side "a deep dull flare like a coal blown on", the arm "a fifth of a beat late"; the stoppage, the healers at a walk, "What day is it?" Nothing is lingered on, and the cruellest thing on any floor is declined twice by the people who could have done it (Lira's hand on the Fenmark boy's chest, ch16; Daeva's slackened air, ch56). No romance and no innuendo: Lira's hand on his head "as she might have on a younger brother's", "like living with a family of clerks", Karis's coat "buttoned one hole wrong all the way down". Wrong is named as wrong by the people wronged and by the book: Fenmark kept her name and threw out her foot; the lean man in brown "wasn't coaching. He was keeping."; "Specimen."; the designation "a drawer somebody had nailed shut and then taken the hammer away"; "they keep a door shut in his face because he frightens them. They hold a door open for her because she pleases them." Kindness is paid for and not rewarded cheaply: the foreman's "It's only angry", the barge-master's "Everybody falls off it first", Zerin's "Good."

## 7. Rhythm outliers — meter only

The book measures 13.65 mean (median 10), 27.2% at five words or fewer, 3.4% at forty or more, 943.5 words a scene, paragraph median 28, all inside the working ranges and nearer the target than Book 4. Fifteen chapters sit under a 13 mean: ch3 (12.4), ch4 (12.78), ch10 (12.46), ch36 (12.56), ch45 (12.33), ch47 (12.61), ch48 (12.59), ch52 (12.43), ch53 (11.57), ch58 (12.16), ch59 (12.89), and the short-sentenced table scenes ch2, ch20, ch34. Read with that question open, every one of them is dialogue-dense or a Log-and-list chapter (ch45's inventory, ch53's eve with its wall of lines and the minute, ch58's hour with its eight words), and the clip is the scene. The two long-sentenced chapters are the two that should be: ch54 (16.02, the first exchange) and ch43 (15.44, Vastin's walk and the rest day). Verdict: meter only.

