  215	"Because it's the only interesting one." Ephram ran his pencil down the column without touching the paper. "Look at it. It goes up and down like an honest man's. Better floors, better figures. A good gallery, a little higher. Bad fish, a little lower. If you showed this to a stranger he'd say, there's a strong Iron with good days and bad ones, and he'd be right." The pencil stopped. "Then look at the top of it."
