    58	
    59	Nobody touched the instrument.
    60	
    61	Withrow broke the wax with her thumbnail and read where she stood, and nobody in the hall would have dared to bring her a chair. She read the first leaf once to herself, without a sign. Then she read it again, aloud, for the hall's book: on service, the enrollee must hear it, and the house must be able to say he had.
    62	
    63	Cael had never heard the voice she used. Two sentences in, he knew it was not new. It was the oldest she owned. Twenty years of registry windows were in it, a clerk's voice that gives a paper to a room exactly as the paper gives itself and adds nothing, not even breath.
    64	
    65	*To the Chancellor, Halcenvane Academy, and to the enrollee of record, Caelen Hesk-ward, unclassified, enrolled under the demonstration provision of the assay clause, jointly:*
    66	
    67	*Be it known that the Guilds Compact, by its registry, having convened formal proceedings upon the question of the classification designated [SHATTERED] and its bearing upon evaluation integrity within chartered institutions, hereby files a formal challenge to enrollment basis against the said enrollment.*
    68	
