     1	# Chapter 9 — Eleven Pounds
     2	
     3	On the thirteenth night of the year the fire-watch's oil book took another line in Bracken's own hand.
     4	
     5	*Library, top floor. Lamps late. On the registrar's authority, and at his charge.*
     6	
     7	Cael saw it in the morning, on his way past the hook by the records-hall side door. Bracken signed that book every morning and almost never wrote in it. Now he had written in it twice in a week. He stood and looked at the page longer than a page of lamp-hours deserved, and then he went up to the top of the library and found out what the lamps had been burning for.
